00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.078
-Thank you for coming.
-Does this feel good or what?

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.113
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.516
This is...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.183
I missed it. But thank you.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:52.885
You were nice enough
to do our show

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.520
when I was doing it
from my home.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.855
-Which was fun.

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.824
This is more fun.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.992
-Or funnest.
-Yeah, it is.

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:01.227
This is the funnest.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.395
-I like nothing more
than a callback.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:06.199
-Hey, I heard a rumor about you.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.268
You may be filming a movie.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:10.903
-Yes. I'm filming a movie.

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.238
-You are, but are you doing --

00:01:13.238 --> 00:01:14.473
-Well, I'll tell you.

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:16.142
Maybe you can guess
what I'm filming.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.977
It starts with an "F."
-Yes.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.379
-And it rhymes with "fletch."
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:22.315
-You are doing "Fletch?"
-We're remaking "Fletch," yes.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.617
We're rebooting Fletch
up in Boston.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.585
We start Monday
and we're very excited.

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:27.687
Greg Mottola is directing.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.790
Myself, John Slattery...
-Holy moly.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.325
-A cast of others will be in it.
-That's major!

00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:34.927
-Very exciting. Very exciting.
-That's genius!

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.195
-Yes. Very, very exciting.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:38.731
It's very exciting.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.166
We all loved the movie
growing up.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:43.536
It's an '80s staple, and we're
gonna sort of reboot it

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.204
and update it for the 2000s.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:46.639
-You're perfect.
-Well, thank you.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:51.411
-I was going to talk about
"Top Gun: Maverick," of course.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.679
-Oh, we can talk about that,
too.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.012
-Yeah. I mean...

00:01:54.012 --> 00:01:57.316
I'm so excited. You've got
some big movies right now.

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:59.785
But "Top Gun: Maverick."

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:02.321
-Well, I think I'm just gonna
go through the '80s

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:05.024
and try to be in all of either
the sequels or the reboots

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.526
of all of those.
-That's smart.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:09.062
-Keep your eyes out
for "Labyrinth."

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:12.098
-Wow, that'll be fantastic.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:14.834
Did you bond with Tom Cruise?
-T.C.? Yes, I did.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.703
-T.C. Wow. They call him T.C.?

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:19.239
-Yeah, well, you know.
-Wow.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.874
-Once you know him,
he's kind of...

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:24.877
No, I had actually met Tom
a long time before.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:28.013
I was a friend's --
Jimmy Kimmel's house.

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:30.383
Another Jimmy.
-He has fun parties.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:33.119
-He has fun parties, and he was
having a football-watching party

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.987
of a Sunday, as you do.

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:38.024
And the rumor got around,

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.560
"Somebody said
Tom Cruise was coming today."

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.794
And everyone was like,
"No, he's not."

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:42.996
It's like,
it's a football party.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.463
We're all watching football.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.432
It's like, a bunch of idiots
eating pizza and drinking beer.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.935
Tom Cruise is not coming
to this football party.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:52.004
Cut to three minutes later,
Tom Cruise walks in

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:53.439
with his mom.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.541
-What?

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:57.643
-Mom Cruise.
-Mom Cruise. Oh, my gosh!

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.745
I didn't even think of that.
Dude, that's genius.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:03.082
Did you start that?
Mom Cruise is the best.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:06.252
-And then cut to
the reverse of this, like,

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.921
40 dudes just with
their jaws on the ground like,

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:10.790
"Is this actually happening?"

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.324
So I did bring that up
when I --

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:13.826
He said, "Yeah, that was
a fun party, man.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.028
We had a great time. Me and my
mom, that was awesome."

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:18.363
-I was like, "You remembered
that. Okay, well."

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:20.499
It was clearly more important
to me than you, but...

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.234
-How was Mom Cruise?

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.403
-Excellent. She can hang.
-And just cool, right?

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:25.971
-Yeah. She can hang.

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:27.206
-I love that. That's fantastic.

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:28.608
-It was a fun, fun time,

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:33.279
and Tom is the most
giving, wonderful guy.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.947
He's the first guy
and the last guy out.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.516
He's the hardest-working guy
on the set.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:37.650
He's always in a good mood.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.218
He's got all
the heavy lifting to do,

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:42.488
including, like, flying planes
at Mach-whatever.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:45.891
And, you know,
it's inspirational.

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:47.159
I'll tell you that much.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.894
-Let's talk about
"No Sudden Move."

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:49.862
-Let's do.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.464
-This is a heist movie.
-Yes.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.665
-I don't want to
give too much away,

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.600
but that's the thing now,
with the...

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.101
-I didn't do it.

00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:57.436
[ Audience laughs ]

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:58.804
-You can't say that.

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:01.074
-Well, no, there's a lot of
other people in the movie.

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.609
-That's not even in question.
-Wasn't me.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.912
-Shaggy's in the movie.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.113
-The rapper or
the cartoon character?

00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:09.782
-[ Laughing ] Both.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.149
-[ As Shaggy ] Oh, no, Scoob!

00:04:11.149 --> 00:04:15.588
We're in a heist movie
directed by Steven Soderbergh!

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.457
[ As Scooby-Doo ] Rokey-doke!

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.292
-Dude, Steven Soderbergh.
Come on.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.895
-Cartoon character is
the obvious answer.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:25.097
-This is great,
when you do impressions.

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:28.100
But what's it like getting
directed by Steven Soderbergh?

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.769
-Well, first of all, we shot
this movie in October,

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:32.672
so it was in
the middle of the pandemic.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:35.541
We shot it in Detroit. The movie
takes place in the '50s.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:39.111
So it's a period film that
has a lot of moving parts,

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.513
a lot of cars,
a lot of costumes,

00:04:41.513 --> 00:04:42.681
a lot of hair and makeup.

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:44.117
Everything that you
wouldn't want to do

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.317
in the middle of a pandemic,

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:49.722
and Steven Soderbergh
was like a conductor.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:52.025
He just, nothing fazed him.

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:54.394
He had this very, very
complicated story

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:55.894
with all these moving parts.

00:04:55.894 --> 00:05:00.332
We would finish in 6-hour days.

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.334
Nobody got sick.
We stayed in a bubble.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.670
Everybody stayed
in the same hotel.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.240
That was very fun, so we all
got to kind of hang out.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.975
It was a lovely, lovely
experience,

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:12.011
and we made a really wonderful
movie with an amazing cast.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.313
-Benicio del Toro.
-Benicio del Toro,

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:16.449
Don Cheadle, Ray Liotta.
-Don Cheadle!

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:19.151
-Myself and people like me.

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.686
-David Harbour. Yeah. Exactly.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:23.489
-Harbour.
-David Harbour.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:24.757
I want to show a clip here.

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:28.160
It is Jon Hamm and David Harbour
in "No Sudden Move."

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.730
Take a look at this.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.930
-Mr. Wertz.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.332
Detective Joe Finney.

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:34.967
Michigan State
Attorney General's office.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.735
Organized crime task force.

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:38.204
-Organized crime?

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:40.939
-Yeah. Uh...

00:05:40.939 --> 00:05:43.843
Detroit police
got two phone calls.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.145
One from a friend,
Mrs. Atkinson,

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.579
said she was concerned,

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:49.715
and then another from a neighbor
said they heard loud noises.

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:52.184
-Organized crime, like the mob?

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:55.221
-Well, I guess that's
the $6,400 question, isn't it?

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:57.423 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.425
-Woo!
-See?

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.627
-Woo!
-Subtle!

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:03.862
-Yes, I love that!
Jon Hamm, everybody!

00:06:03.862 --> 00:06:04.864
-Subtle!

